  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e67cd6817dcb29f468d27d58fdd355ca, type: 3}
  m_Name: ForestDrainage
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  stage: 2
  stageName: ForestDrainage
  facts:
  - factText: In natural areas, some water seeps into the soil and slowly travels
      through dirt, rock, and underground spaces.
    narrationClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: ee1b7c35aacb5734cae548371df8603b, type: 3}
    displayDuration: 0
    waitForAudio: 1
    delayBeforeShow: 0
  - factText: This groundwater can flow through caves or collect in underground reservoirs
      called aquifers.
    narrationClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: e00ae4ec281d1e44786ab2b864fdffb1, type: 3}
    displayDuration: 0
    waitForAudio: 1
    delayBeforeShow: 0
  - factText: Later, it may emerge from springs or feed rivers and wetlands.
    narrationClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a73b10bfb161cbe429f152292a17316c, type: 3}
    displayDuration: 0
    waitForAudio: 1
    delayBeforeShow: 0
  - factText: "Water finds its way\u2014now flowing toward the next stage: River."
    narrationClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7e5eba0becef8aa429538ca2ffdc452c, type: 3}
    displayDuration: 0
    waitForAudio: 1
    delayBeforeShow: 0
  defaultFactDuration: 5
  timeBetweenFacts: 1
